I'd like to talk about a memorable cake that I received from my friends on my birthday last year.

The celebration took place at a cozy café in the city center. I wasn't expecting anything unusual because we had simply planned to have dinner together and spend some time catching up. However, toward the end of the evening, my friends suddenly brought out a cake and started singing "Happy Birthday," which completely caught me by surprise.

The cake was a bento cake, which has become quite popular in recent years. It's much smaller than a traditional birthday cake and is known for its cute and simple design. What made this one stand out was that it was decorated with tiny fondant flowers and a miniature cat figure because my friends know how much I love cats. They had even written my name on top in a colorful and playful style.

